    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes along with a clean full build (all main + test sources compiled). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule \"reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner \u2192 409\", mirroring the existing duplicate-telephone handling so each piece of logic lives where it belongs:\n\n1. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added `existsByEmailIgnoreCase(String email)` to the interface, alongside the existing `existsByTelephone`.\n\n2. **Three repository implementations** \u2014 added the case-insensitive existence check:\n   - `SpringDataOwnerRepository` \u2014 derived query method.\n   - `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 JPQL with `LOWER(...)`.\n   - `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` \u2014 SQL with `LOWER(...)`.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailException`** \u2014 new domain exception, matching `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n4. **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 added the check right after the telephone check, guarded on a non-null email (email is optional, so owners without one are unaffected). The email is already normalized to lower-case by `OwnerMapper`/`EmailNormalizer`, and the repository comparison is case-insensitive for defense in depth.\n\n5. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DuplicateEmailException` to `409 Conflict`, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes and the full build is green.",
